              "current_clause_status": "current"
            }
          },
          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§13.7",
            "section_heading": "Metadata Standard and Operations Interface",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 13.7 Metadata Standard and Operations Interface\n\nDetailed metadata templates, controlled-value catalogues, registry rendering rules, parser behaviour, validator implementation, schema mapping, and maintenance workflows SHALL be governed by the applicable governance metadata standard, OPERATIONS instrument, registry schedule, schema file, or automation specification.\n\nNo metadata standard, OPERATIONS instrument, registry schedule, schema, validator, generator, or automation may weaken, collapse, or bypass the constitutional separation rules established in this Article.\n\nWhere a metadata standard changes controlled vocabulary, field interpretation, field ordering, parser expectations, registry rendering, or validator behaviour, the change SHALL identify affected instruments and trigger corpus review where stale constitutional, charter, registry, or schema references may result.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md",
              "direct_url": "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Caelestis/blob/9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467/Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md"
            },
            "verification": {
              "status": "verified-canonical",
              "verified_on": "2026-07-26",
              "review_id": "VIGIL-REVIEW-2026-07-26-CODEX-COVERAGE-0029",
              "exact_text_match": true,
              "current_clause_status": "current"
            }
          },
          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§13.8",
            "section_heading": "Constitutional Corpus Review Requirement",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 13.8 Constitutional Corpus Review Requirement\n\nWhere an amendment, refactor, restructure, reclassification, metadata migration, schema migration, registry update, canonical-code change, or deterministic corpus-wide update affects more than one instrument, domain, annex, schedule, appendix, supplement, framework, policy, index, registry, schema, or generated governance file, the change SHALL be subject to constitutional corpus review before release or final merge.\n\nConstitutional corpus review SHALL assess, at minimum:\n\n* contradiction with higher-order constitutional provisions;\n* stale or broken doctrinal references;\n* annex, appendix, schedule, supplement, and domain-placement drift;\n* metadata-header inconsistency;\n* provenance-footer inconsistency;\n* amendment-ledger discontinuity;\n* canonical-code and reference-set drift;\n* registry and schema mismatch;\n* validator drift;\n* seal misapplication;\n* machine-readability failure;\n* domain-boundary collision;\n* authority-role ambiguity;\n* lifecycle, effect, and governance-standard inconsistency;\n* and logic shear across instruments.\n\nThis review is distinct from ordinary CI.\n\nOrdinary CI may verify syntax, links, schema shape, file presence, parser output, and registry generation. Constitutional corpus review evaluates whether the doctrine remains coherent after change.\n\nWhere review identifies unresolved contradiction, malformed primitive logic, source-authority conflict, stale doctrine, registry-facing inconsistency, or load-bearing cross-instrument drift, the change SHALL be paused, repaired, downgraded to review status, or routed through the applicable arbitration, Tendeka, OPERATIONS, or evidence-to-repair pathway.\n\nNo refactor SHALL be treated as complete merely because the amended instrument is internally readable. Corpus-level coherence is required where the amended material participates in cross-instrument governance.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md",
              "direct_url": "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Caelestis/blob/9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467/Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-001-PLATINUM.md"
            },
