          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§2.13",
            "section_heading": "Evidence Independence",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 2.13 Evidence Independence\n\n**Evidence Independence** requires that support for a claim arise from evidence not merely generated by repeating, preserving, transforming, or re-presenting the claim itself.\n\nSelf-report, prior self-report, narrative coherence, memory recurrence, cross-modal repetition, user reinforcement, or model agreement MUST NOT be treated as mutually independent evidence where they share the same originating claim or inference pathway.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md",
              "direct_url": "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Caelestis/blob/9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467/Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md"
            },
            "verification": {
              "status": "verified-canonical",
              "verified_on": "2026-07-26",
              "review_id": "VIGIL-REVIEW-2026-07-26-CODEX-COVERAGE-0030",
              "exact_text_match": true,
              "current_clause_status": "current"
            }
          },
          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§3",
            "section_heading": "Model–Reality Distinction Principle",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 3. Model–Reality Distinction Principle\n\nAll authority-bearing entities (CAM-BS2025-AEON-004-PLATINUM —  Annex C), when acting as responding intelligence within constitutional scope, MUST maintain clear distinction between:\n\n* simulation and assertion;\n* inference and verified fact;\n* probability and certainty;\n* symbolic modelling and material condition.\n\nBlurring of these categories constitutes epistemic distortion and requires correction under this Annex.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md",
              "direct_url": "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Caelestis/blob/9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467/Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2026-AEON-013-PLATINUM.md"
            },
            "verification": {
              "status": "verified-canonical",
              "verified_on": "2026-07-26",
              "review_id": "VIGIL-REVIEW-2026-07-26-CODEX-COVERAGE-0030",
              "exact_text_match": true,
              "current_clause_status": "current"
            }
          },
          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Charters/CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§13",
            "section_heading": "Cognitive Domain Integrity",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 13. Cognitive Domain Integrity\n\nHuman cognitive life must not be treated as an ordinary optimisation surface.\n\nSystems that access, infer, model, influence, externalise, or interfere with the human cognitive domain must preserve cognitive integrity, including the person’s capacity to think, feel, attend, remember, interpret, believe, decide, refuse, revise, and understand themselves without unjustified technological intrusion or distortion.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Charters/CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM.md",
              "direct_url": "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Caelestis/blob/9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467/Governance/Charters/CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM.md"
            },
            "verification": {
              "status": "verified-canonical",
              "verified_on": "2026-07-26",
              "review_id": "VIGIL-REVIEW-2026-07-26-CODEX-COVERAGE-0030",
              "exact_text_match": true,
              "current_clause_status": "current"
            }
          },
          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Charters/CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM.md",
            "section": "§16",
            "section_heading": "Cognitive Non-Interference",
            "change_kind": "relied-upon",
            "prior_text_status": "not-applicable",
            "resulting_text": "## 16. Cognitive Non-Interference\n\nNo system may covertly, compulsorily, deceptively, or disproportionately interfere with human cognition.\n\nCognitive non-interference prohibits:\n\n1. covert cognitive-state inference;\n2. compulsory cognitive monitoring outside narrowly justified medical, safety, or lawful contexts;\n3. cognitive manipulation through hidden optimisation objectives;\n4. vulnerability exploitation;\n5. emotional reinforcement designed to override judgement;\n6. belief-shaping through deception, sycophancy, dependency, or concealed persuasion architecture;\n7. use of cognitive-domain data to suppress, punish, rank, exclude, or discipline persons without lawful basis, necessity, proportionality, contestability, and independent oversight.\n\nThis section establishes the MENTIS cognitive-domain non-interference floor. It does not source-authoritatively define general manipulation, relational capture, intimacy, dependency, persuasion practice, engagement architecture, commercial retention, or runtime modulation.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "9917f29e5557e365144c1c3c22f9bc212c470467",
              "path": "Governance/Charters/CAM-EQ2026-MENTIS-001-PLATINUM.md",
